lpha\\\",\\\"Consulting\\\",\\\"QA-REF-001\\\",\\\"+$420.50\\\",\\\"✓\\\"] — all supplied values retained.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Editing a transaction silently wipes its category\", \"actual\": \"The Edit Transaction dialog does not pre-populate the Category field — it shows the placeholder \\\"Select category\\\" even though the transaction had Category=Consulting (the hidden select defaults to cat-1). After changing only Description and Amount and clicking \\\"Update Income\\\", the saved row lost its category entirely: cells became [\\\"Aug 20, 2026\\\",\\\"QA Test Income Alpha EDITED\\\",\\\"\\\",\\\"QA-REF-001\\\",\\\"+$500.75\\\",\\\"\\\",\\\"\\\"] — Category is now blank. Description/amount/tax changes did apply, and Delete works correctly.\", \"evidence\": \"Pre-edit row: [\\\"Aug 20, 2026\\\",\\\"QA Test Income Alpha\\\",\\\"Consulting\\\",\\\"QA-REF-001\\\",\\\"+$420.50\\\",\\\"✓\\\"]. Edit dialog combobox text = \\\"Select category\\\". Post-edit Category cell = \\\"\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Created \\\"QA Test Category\\\" (Type=Income, Purple) → appeared under Income Categories (4→5) with purple swatch rgba(168,85,247). Edited to \\\"QA Renamed Category\\\" with Orange → name and swatch rgba(249,115,22) updated. Deleted → removed, Income Categories back to 4.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Assigned category not retained through an edit\", \"actual\": \"Category options are correctly filtered by type (Income → Sales Revenue/Consulting/Interest Income/Other Income; Expense → Office Supplies/Rent/Utilities/etc.) and the category is retained on creation. However the Edit Transaction dialog does not load the transaction's existing category (shows \\\"Select category\\\"), and saving an unrelated field change dropped the assigned \\\"Consulting\\\" category, leaving the transaction's Category cell blank.\", \"evidence\": \"Row Category went from \\\"Consulting\\\" to \\\"\\\" after editing only Description and Amount.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Created transaction with Tax Related switch ON → Tax column showed \\\"✓\\\". Edited the same transaction turning the switch OFF → Tax column became blank. Both create-time and update-time marking/unmarking are honored.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Combined search=\\\"Website\\\" + Type=Income + Category=Consulting + 2024-12-01..2024-12-31 returned exactly 1 row (Dec 1, 2024 Client Project - Website Redesign, Consulting, +$5,500.00) satisfying all criteria. \\\"Clear Filters\\\" restored all 19 transactions with filters reset to All Types/All Categories and empty dates/search.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing required fields are not identified to the user\", \"actual\": \"Submitting Add Transaction with empty description/amount silently does nothing: the dialog stays open, no toast, no inline error text, and no aria-invalid/error styling on any field. The user gets zero feedback about what is missing.\", \"evidence\": \"Clicked \\\"Add Expense\\\" with all fields empty, then again with only Description filled. Dialog innerText contained no \\\"required\\\"/error text; toast region empty.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Invalid date range (start &gt; end) accepted without rejection or explanation\", \"actual\": \"Set From=2024-12-31 and To=2024-12-01. Both values were accepted, no validation error, warning, toast or explanation was shown. The table simply rendered an empty result with the generic message \\\"No transactions found / Try adjusting your filters\\\", which does not identify the invalid range.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-23\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Transaction created with no category; no validation and blank category displayed\", \"actual\": \"Submitted Add Transaction with Description=\\\"Validation Test No Amount\\\", Amount=10 and Category left at \\\"Select category\\\". The dialog closed and the transaction was created. Its Category cell renders as an empty string (blank), leaving a transaction with no category. No error message was shown.\", \"evidence\": \"New row cells: [\\\"Aug 28, 2026\\\",\\\"Validation Test No Amount\\\",\\\"\\\",\\\"—\\\",\\\"-$10.00\\\",\\\"\\\",\\\"\\\"] — 3rd cell (Category) is empty.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-24\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Deleting an in-use category is neither blocked nor requires reassignment, orphaning transactions\", \"actual\": \"Deleted the \\\"Software\\\" expense category which had 1 transaction. The confirm dialog only warned \\\"Transactions using this category will not be deleted\\\" — no block and no reassignment option. After deletion, the transaction \\\"Software Subscription - Adobe CC\\\" (Dec 15, 2024) now renders with an empty/blank Category cell.\", \"evidence\": \"Expense Categories count went 8→7; orphaned row cells: [\\\"Dec 15, 2024\\\",\\\"Software Subscription - Adobe CC\\\",\\\"\\\",\\\"—\\\",\\\"-$54.99\\\",\\\"✓\\\"].\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"ADD: creating Aug 2026 income $420.50 changed Dashboard Monthly Income $0→$421 and Net $0→$421 and placed it top of Recent Transactions. UPDATE: editing it to $500.75 moved Monthly Income to $501; adding a $200.25 Aug expense gave Income $501 / Expenses $200 / Net $301 and Reports Aug 2026 $500.75 / $200.25 / +$300.5. DELETE: removing the expense immediately returned Monthly Expenses to $0, Net to $501, and dropped it from Recent Transactions. All without page reload.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"With the Aug 2026 transaction unmarked, the 2026 Tax Summary showed Total Taxable Income $0.00 and \\\"No tax-related transactions for 2026\\\". After re-marking it Tax Related (row Tax cell → \\\"✓\\\"), the 2026 summary showed Total Taxable Income $500.75, Net Taxable Income $500.75, Consulting $500.75 (100%), and \\\"1 transactions\\\" listing it.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Consulting was 3 txns/$10,800 before; after creating a $420.50 Consulting income it read 4 txns/$11,220.50; after editing that transaction to $500.75 it updated to 4 txns/$11,300.75 (1800+5500+3500+500.75). Deleting a transaction likewise restored prior counts.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicked \\\"Print Report\\\" for year 2024; window.print() was invoked exactly once and the page remained fully rendered with no application error (only a pre-existing React dev \\\"unique key prop\\\" warning in TaxSummary).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Transactions table columns: Date, Description, Category, Reference, Amount, Tax, Actions. Footer shows Total Income +$48,013.00 and Total Expenses -$36,485.99 for the current result set.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Underlying Aug 2026 transactions: +$500.75 (Consulting) and -$200.25 (Office Supplies). Dashboard showed Monthly Income $501, Monthly Expenses $200, Net Profit/Loss $301 (rounded from $300.50); Recent Transactions listed both with correct dates/categories/amounts. Reports → August 2026 showed Total Income $500.75, Total Expenses $200.25, Net +$300.5, Income by Category Consulting $500.75, Expenses by Category Office Supplies $200.25 — all matching exactly.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Chart Y-axis labels lack precision; non-zero amounts render as \\\"$0k\\\"\", \"actual\": \"After adding an Aug 2026 income of $420.50, the \\\"Income vs Expenses\\\" chart plots a non-zero bar for Aug, but 4 of its 5 Y-axis tick labels read \\\"$0k\\\" (the 5th reads \\\"$1k\\\"). A $420.50 value is indistinguishable from $0 on the axis — the \\\"$Nk\\\" formatting truncates all values below $500 to $0k.\", \"evidence\": \"Y-axis ticks: [\\\"$0k\\\",\\\"$0k\\\",\\\"$0k\\\",\\\"$0k\\\",\\\"$1k\\\"] for a series whose only non-zero point is $420.50.\"}]}"
