    "content": "All 22 checklist items have been executed and recorded — testing is complete.\n\n**Summary: 16 PASS / 6 FAIL**\n\nThe core bookkeeping features work well: transaction CRUD, type/category/date/search filtering (including correctly combined criteria), category management with color and type, the annual tax summary with breakdowns and printing, and live-updating dashboards, reports, and category rollups.\n\nSix defects were confirmed:\n\n| ID | Defect |\n|---|---|\n| **CS-13** | Submitting the Add Transaction form with missing description/amount does nothing at all — no toast, no inline error, no field highlighting. |\n| **CS-23** | A transaction can be saved with **no category** at all; it is created silently and renders with a blank Category cell. |\n| **FT-7 / FT-9** | The Edit Transaction dialog never pre-populates the Category field. Editing any other field (e.g. description) silently **wipes the transaction's category**. |\n| **CS-24** | Deleting a category that is in use is neither blocked nor offers reassignment — it orphans transactions, which then show blank in the table and \"Unknown\" in the tax summary. |\n| **CT-22** | Chart Y-axis labels use `$Nk` formatting, so any value under $500 renders as `$0k` — a plotted $420.50 bar is indistinguishable from zero. |\n\nThe most impactful issue is the category-wipe on edit (FT-7/FT-9) combined with the lack of category validation (CS-23) and unguarded category deletion (CS-24), which together allow financial records to silently lose their categorization and corrupt the category-based reports and tax summaries."
  }
